IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ia-types`

-- Insurance Act 2015 (UK) — GOAL 3: WARRANTIES, OTHER TERMS AND FRAUDULENT
-- CLAIMS (ss 10, 11, 12).
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-2015-4.txt.

§ `Goal 3 — warranties, other terms and fraud`

-- s 10(2) "An insurer has no liability under a contract of insurance in
-- respect of any loss occurring, or attributable to something happening,
-- after a warranty (express or implied) in the contract has been breached but
-- before the breach has been remedied." (3) "But subsection (2) does not
-- apply if— (a) because of a change of circumstances, the warranty ceases to
-- be applicable to the circumstances of the contract, (b) compliance with the
-- warranty is rendered unlawful by any subsequent law, or (c) the insurer
-- waives the breach of warranty." (4): losses before the breach, or after it
-- has been remedied, are unaffected. A loss on the day of breach or the day
-- of remedy is not "after ... but before".
@ref s 10(2)-(5)
@export Whether a breach of warranty suspends the insurer's liability for a loss under s 10 of the Insurance Act 2015 (UK): the loss occurred after the warranty was breached and before the breach was remedied (or it has not been), unless the warranty ceased to apply by a change of circumstances, compliance became unlawful, or the insurer waived the breach. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN b IS A `Warranty breach`  @desc The day of breach, the day of remedy if any, and the s 10(3) exceptions
      d IS A DATE               @desc The day of the loss, or of what it is attributable to
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the breach of warranty` b `suspends liability for a loss on` d IF
        d GREATER THAN b's `breached on`
    AND beforeRemedy
    AND NOT (b's `ceased to be applicable by a change of circumstances`)
    AND NOT (b's `compliance made unlawful by a later law`)
    AND NOT (b's `the insurer waived the breach`)
    WHERE
        beforeRemedy MEANS
            CONSIDER b's `remedied on`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
            WHEN JUST r  THEN d LESS THAN r

-- s 11(1)-(3): for a term (other than one defining the risk as a whole)
-- whose compliance would tend to reduce the risk of loss of a particular
-- kind, at a particular location or at a particular time, "the insurer may
-- not rely on the non-compliance to exclude, limit or discharge its liability
-- ... if the insured ... shows that the non-compliance with the term could
-- not have increased the risk of the loss which actually occurred in the
-- circumstances in which it occurred."
@ref s 11
@export Whether the insurer may rely on the insured's non-compliance with a term to exclude, limit or discharge its liability for a loss, under s 11 of the Insurance Act 2015 (UK): it may, unless the term (not one defining the risk as a whole) would tend to reduce the risk of loss of a particular kind, place or time and the insured shows the non-compliance could not have increased the risk of the loss that occurred. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN t IS A `Term non-compliance`  @desc The kind of term and what the insured shows
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the insurer may rely on the non-compliance in` t IF
    NOT (    NOT (t's `the term defines the risk as a whole`)
         AND t's `compliance would tend to reduce the risk of loss of a particular kind, place or time`
         AND t's `the insured shows it could not have increased the risk of the actual loss`)

-- s 12(1) "If the insured makes a fraudulent claim ... (a) the insurer is not
-- liable to pay the claim, (b) the insurer may recover from the insured any
-- sums paid by the insurer to the insured in respect of the claim, and (c) in
-- addition, the insurer may by notice to the insured treat the contract as
-- having been terminated with effect from the time of the fraudulent act."
-- (2) "(a) it may refuse all liability ... in respect of a relevant event
-- occurring after the time of the fraudulent act, and (b) it need not return
-- any of the premiums paid". (3): events before it are unaffected.
@ref s 12(1)-(4)
@export Whether fraud excludes the insurer's liability for a claim under s 12 of the Insurance Act 2015 (UK): the claim is itself fraudulent, or the insurer has treated the contract as terminated from an earlier fraudulent act and the claim's relevant event occurred after it. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN f IS A `Fraud facts`  @desc Whether this claim is fraudulent, and the time of any fraudulent act from which the contract was treated as terminated
      d IS A DATE           @desc The day of the relevant event the claim is for
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `fraud excludes liability under` f `for an event on` d IF
        f's `this claim is fraudulent`
    OR  afterTermination
    WHERE
        afterTermination MEANS
            CONSIDER f's `terminated from a fraudulent act on`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST t  THEN d GREATER THAN t

@ref s 12(1)(b)
GIVEN f IS A `Fraud facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the sums the insurer may recover under` f MEANS
    IF f's `this claim is fraudulent` THEN f's `sums already paid on this claim` ELSE 0
